{
  "id": "ss.enemy.bristle",
  "name": "Bristle",
  "description": "The burrow's fast chaff — a silverfish out of the wall seams, running the nest's trails and stealing off them, the one thing down here that does not belong to the hive. Drawn from the side and mirrored by the game. Long and low, because that is what a silverfish is: the body's half-height is capped at 2.5 against a length of nineteen, where an earlier cut drew it 4.5 deep and came out a sausage. The silhouette is a comet — a flat plated body dragging a fan half again its own length, which nothing else in the game is. The three caudal filaments are fused into one plume rather than drawn as three rods, since five thin rods off a small oval is an asterisk at the size this is seen at, and the notches keep them legible as three. There is one skeleton and everything hangs off it. Nine spine segments chained head to tail, each joint carrying a share of the wave that arrives later and larger the further back it is; a tergite rides each segment; every leg hip rides the joint it attaches to and the leg solves from wherever that joint has moved; the plume, its hairs and its collar hang off the tail joint and inherit its bearing; the head cap, frons, eye, jaw, palp and both antennae are placed by rotating about the neck. An earlier pass gave each part its own sine and you could see between them at the extremes of the cycle. Nothing here is free-floating, so nothing can come apart. Cool silver against a roster of warm bone and amber so it never competes with the Replete or the Porter's brood, and the palest body on it — this runs on #372d3f earth and the quickest thing on screen must not be the hardest to see. Gameplay radius 7.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "bristle"],
  "size": [48, 24],
  "meta": {"radius": 7},
